---
description: User-facing copy must not use dashes, dots or arrows as separators inside sentences
alwaysApply: true
---

# No separator symbols in user-facing copy

Applies to every visible string: templates, UI labels, data files (`mock-data.ts`,
`photographers.json`, page `.ts` arrays), SEO titles and descriptions.

Never use these as separators inside text:

- Em dash `—` and en dash `–`
- Middle dot `·` or bullet `•` between words or values
- Arrow chains like `Book → Match → Deliver`
- Slashes as "or", like `Custom / corporate`

Use normal punctuation instead: a period, a comma, a colon, or the words
"and", "or", "to", "in", "with".

```text
❌ Any event or party — pick type, place, and time.
✅ Any event or party. Pick type, place, and time.

❌ Menus · restaurants · delivery apps
✅ Menus, restaurants and delivery apps

❌ 2–4 hours          ✅ 2 to 4 hours
❌ Sony · Lenses      ✅ Sony in Lenses   (or two separately styled elements)
❌ BookMyCamera — Pro Photography   ✅ BookMyCamera: Pro Photography
```

When UI needs to show several short values side by side (brand and category,
specs), render them as separate elements spaced with CSS `gap` instead of
joining them with a symbol. Do not add symbols through CSS `content` either.

Allowed: `₹`, `%`, `★` for ratings, and a single trailing arrow icon on a link
or button label (for example "View pricing →").

Placeholders for empty values use words ("Not set"), never a dash.
